  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 200 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nTuesday through Saturday:\n\nOverall the extended period look very quiet with the pattern\nremaining fairly meridional with weak troughing to the east and\nweak ridging to the west. It remains very stagnant pattern\noverall. While this type of pattern would generally lead to some\nactivity aloft in the shortwave department, models keeping\nthings largely quiet. At the surface, a low pressure system will\nswing across the northern Great Lakes Tuesday into Wednesday\ndragging a front across the region, but this front (at this\ntime) looks quiet dry with limited moisture in the low to mid\nlevels. The front may carry a slight chance for precip Tuesday\nnight into Wednesday morning but forcing will be limited in\naddition to limited moisture.\n\nWeak high pressure will work back into the region late Wednesday\nthrough Thursday likely keeping the area dry. Then into Friday\nis where we see increased model divergence with a few models\npointing toward some introduction of precip chances attached to\na warm front. However, models differ greatly on the extent of\nthe low pressure to the west and the potential for it to extend\ntoward the Great Lakes. In any case it is something to monitor \nthough chances overall remain slim. We will be monitoring a \npotential break in the pattern into early next week.\n\nOtherwise, relatively cool conditions expected overall with\npotential for patchy frost in spots over the next week.\n\nKuroski",
